(version 1)

# DrikrAIO design rules.
#
# Custom rules only. The fab numbers that gate an order live in the project file
# under board.design_settings.rules. The line standard inherited from the
# OpenDrone template is:
#
#   clearance 0.09   track 0.09   via 0.35 / 0.20 drill
#   annular 0.075    hole-to-hole 0.20        edge clearance 0.20
#
# Do not restate those here. Two copies of a number drift, and the one you are
# not looking at is the one that is wrong.

(rule "silkscreen over pad"
  (constraint silk_clearance (min 0.15mm))
  (condition "A.Type == 'Pad'"))

# --- board-specific rules below this line ------------------------------------

# 2 OZ OUTER COPPER. Four 40 V power stages plus a 115 A-capable battery entry.
# Heavier copper etches with a wider taper, so outer layers need 0.16 mm where
# the line standard is 0.09 mm. Inner layers stay at 1 oz and keep the standard.
#
# This is a rule and not a global minimum on purpose: raising the board minimum
# would constrain inner-layer signal routing for no reason. Anything narrower
# than 0.16 mm (USB pair, Analog, Default) routes on the inner layers or gets
# widened where it surfaces.
#
# THE STACK-UP MUST AGREE. OpenAIO enforced these same 0.16 mm rules while its
# stack-up declared 1 oz outer, so traces were sized for copper the fabricator
# was never asked to supply. Check board setup, not just this file.

(rule "2 oz outer copper, clearance"
  (constraint clearance (min 0.16mm))
  (layer outer))

(rule "2 oz outer copper, track width"
  (constraint track_width (min 0.16mm))
  (layer outer))

# MOTOR PHASE AND BATTERY COPPER.
#
# Calculated in tools/power_review.py, not chosen. IPC-2221 on 2 oz outer at a
# 20 C rise gives 5.3 A for a 1.0 mm track. Phase RMS is 21 A at hover and 29 A
# at peak; the bus is 42 A continuous. The old 1.0 mm floor was inherited from
# OpenAIO, a toothpick-class board, and was short by 4-6x -- it would have
# passed DRC on a board that could not carry its own current.
#
# 6.6 mm is the PER-LAYER minimum for 21 A. The rated current is reached by
# pouring the same net on all six layers and stitching them; these rules are a
# floor that stops a hand-route necking down where it leaves a pad, not a
# statement that one 6.6 mm trace is the whole conductor.

(rule "motor phase minimum width"
  (constraint track_width (min 6.6mm))
  (condition "A.NetClass == 'Phase'"))

(rule "battery rail minimum width"
  (constraint track_width (min 6.6mm))
  (condition "A.NetClass == 'VBAT'"))

# HIGH-CURRENT VIAS.
# 0.3 mm drill at 25 um plating is 1.08 mohm and about 1.5 A continuous. The bus
# needs 28 vias at 42 A and 38 at 115 A; a phase needs 14. Single vias on these
# nets are the bottleneck the pours exist to avoid, so the minimum via is
# enlarged and the array requirement is documented in the design review.

(rule "power via size"
  (constraint via_diameter (min 0.8mm))
  (condition "A.NetClass == 'Phase' || A.NetClass == 'VBAT'"))

# RF KEEP-CLEAR, 2.4 GHz ELRS.
# The receiver chain shares a board with four switching power stages. Copper
# pours and other nets stay back from the RF net so the transmission line keeps
# a clean reference. None of the OpenDrone RF boards declared an impedance
# constraint at all -- this is the minimum that makes the intent enforceable.

(rule "RF clearance to other copper"
  (constraint clearance (min 0.30mm))
  (condition "A.NetClass == 'RF' && B.NetClass != 'RF'"))
